              "id": "2848473f-3d42-443d-bb88-12e5c392f19e",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Shakespeare the Boy: With Sketches of the Home &amp; School Life the Games &amp; Sports, the Manners, Customs &amp; Folk-Lore of the Time</strong></em> was written by William Rolfe, originally published by Chatto, January 1, 1897."
            },
            {
              "id": "204ec26a-4109-48e0-9160-7070eb9abe61",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "8ba47421-74a5-4d76-9408-df92b36b0db0",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Two years ago, at the request of the editors of the Youtz's Companion, I wrote for that periodical a series Of four familiar articles on the boyhood of Shakespeare. It was understood at the time that I might afterwards ex pand them into a book, and this plan is carried out in the present volume. The papers have been carefully revised and enlarged to thrice their original compass, and a new fifth chapter has been added.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "62d5b647-f106-4575-ab56-e55c8049a4cf",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
